Further reading",[90,91],{"_51":94,"_25":95},{"_51":92,"_25":93},"Versioned test-job and cancellation API","https://docs.unity3d.com/Packages/com.unity.test-framework@1.4/api/UnityEditor.TestTools.TestRunner.Api.TestRunnerApi.html","Package and API documentation","https://docs.unity3d.com/Packages/com.unity.test-framework@latest/","Project source",[98],{"_51":96,"_25":99},"https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.2/Documentation/Manual/test-framework/test-framework-introduction.html","Why it belongs here","Enables ongoing regression checks for generated scripts and scene behavior, using UnityTest across frames to check lifecycles, coroutines, and state changes. Edit mode and Play mode have different execution loops; tests should wait for real frames or conditions rather than only confirming script creation. The separately checked Test Framework 1.4.6 API returns a job GUID and documents multi-frame cancellation cleanup. Active tests become Canceled and remaining tests NotRun; do not equate cancellation with passing or assume compatibility with every Editor package version.","detail","guidance","Resource type","Tool","Category","Engines & creation tools","category","lead","summary","name","engines","tool",[123,124],[56,80,85,86,87],[120,121,122],[118,119],"2d","3d","code","test","ship",{"_51":94,"_25":95},{"_51":92,"_25":93},{"_126":127},"documents",{"_128":129,"_130":131},"en",[133,137,138,139,136,140,141,142,143,144,145,146,147,148,149,150,151,152,153,154,155,156,157,158,159,160,161,162,163,164,165,166,167,168,169,170,171,135,172,134,173,174,175,176,177,178,179,180,181,182,183,184,185,186,187,188,189,190,191,192,193],"zh",[132,133,134,135,136],"reading-guide","practical-guide","level-design-skill","deployment","publishing-platforms","tutorials-and-demos","coding-agent-game-code","game-testing-library","agents-notes","engines-notes","game-ai-notes","cadle-repositories","world-model-notes","research-index","production-research-notes","engine-operation-contracts","production-wor